                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c4cb689a-b04f-3868-9c2e-1997917f2988",
                        "entry_id": "ed49b9f9-948b-34e8-b43f-4a2415d3b0c9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To defecate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b00929d8-d7d7-4411-9c7e-5ee7f204965f",
                                "sense_id": "c4cb689a-b04f-3868-9c2e-1997917f2988",
                                "text": "But he that gaines the glory here Muſt ſcumber furtheſt, ſhite moſt clear."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ee61a1e-3822-46f6-8300-8805c024cf22",
                                "sense_id": "c4cb689a-b04f-3868-9c2e-1997917f2988",
                                "text": "Beware of fire when you ſcumber, Though to ſh-- [shit] fire were a wonder,"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a0fd92c-5220-4cdd-b8b2-b4a5ce7139e0",
                                "sense_id": "c4cb689a-b04f-3868-9c2e-1997917f2988",
                                "text": "[…]and old Nick turn me into Bumfodder, if this did not make me ſo hide-bound and coſtive; that for four or five Days I hardly ſcumber'd one poor Butt of Sir-reverance and that too was full as dry and hard, I protest"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "40ce7ffa-ea9f-403b-aba6-8957e8333484",
                                "sense_id": "c4cb689a-b04f-3868-9c2e-1997917f2988",
                                "text": "He’s not to come in the house, though, Natasha. Other than to scumber, I suppose. / What? / To disencumber. His bowels."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2ed6f70d-9627-3955-84c1-9ab793377efc",
                        "entry_id": "ed49b9f9-948b-34e8-b43f-4a2415d3b0c9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To defecate.",
                            "of a dog or fox"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9d61620-caa6-49dc-9b79-ddb7f3aab546",
                                "sense_id": "2ed6f70d-9627-3955-84c1-9ab793377efc",
                                "text": "Some tyme pei han a siknesse bat pei mowe not pisse and byn ilost therbi, and also whan pei mowe not scombire",
                                "translation": "Sometimes the hounds have a great sickness that they may not piss, and be lost thereby and also when they may not scumber.",
                                "english": "Sometimes the hounds have a great sickness that they may not piss, and be lost thereby and also when they may not scumber."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "51276b78-905f-40d3-9321-650f3755c0c4",
                                "sense_id": "2ed6f70d-9627-3955-84c1-9ab793377efc",
                                "text": "a brace of gray-houndes When they are ledd out of their kennels to ſcumber"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ec4f974-cdf9-4a27-a1c3-37bfb413e2da",
                                "sense_id": "2ed6f70d-9627-3955-84c1-9ab793377efc",
                                "text": "But that their beds were heav'd on high ; They thought some dog under did lie, And meant i' th' chamber (fie, fie, fie,) To scumber."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
